# SCF-Scaffald Workspace Commands Reference

## Quick Reference: Fast Iteration vs. Full Validation

### Fast Iteration Loop (During Development)
Use affected commands for 2-5x faster feedback while coding:

```bash
# Make changes → Run affected checks
pnpm check:affected       # Lint and type check only changed packages
pnpm lint:affected        # Lint only changed packages
pnpm typecheck:affected   # Type check only changed packages
```

**When to use:**
- During active development
- After implementing features
- When fixing bugs
- For quick feedback cycles
- While iterating on code

### Pre-Commit Validation (Before Commit)
Run comprehensive validation before committing or marking work complete:

```bash
# Final validation before commit
pnpm lint:fix             # Auto-fix linting issues
pnpm check                # Lint and type check all packages
pnpm build                # Verify everything builds
pnpm check-deps           # Dependency consistency
```

**When to use:**
- Before committing changes
- Before creating pull requests
- Before marking BrainGrid tasks COMPLETED
- Before merging branches
- When work is "done"

### Why This Matters
- **Fast iteration**: Affected checks are 2-5x faster, focusing only on changed code
- **Quality assurance**: Full checks ensure nothing breaks in unrelated packages
- **Nx caching**: Reuses results for unchanged packages
- **Best of both worlds**: Speed during development, thoroughness before commit

